---
// Install: the three ways onto a phone, as they stand. The desktop app
// reinstalls, the web page checks and writes nothing, and first installs go
// through the command line. Keep each claim to what has run on hardware
// (the installer repository's docs/GO-LIVE.md, and docs/INSTALL.md here).
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { REPO_URL } from "../../lib/devices";

const INSTALLER_REPO = "https://github.com/derekross/omamobile-installer";
const APP_RELEASE = `${INSTALLER_REPO}/releases/tag/v0.1.0`;
const APP_DOCS = `${INSTALLER_REPO}/blob/main/docs/INSTALL-APP.md`;
const WEB_APP = "/install/web/app/";
const INSTALL_DOC = `${REPO_URL}/blob/main/docs/INSTALL.md`;
const GUIDED_DOC = `${REPO_URL}/blob/main/docs/INSTALL-GUIDED.md`;
---
<Base title="Install" description="Install Omarchy Mobile on your phone: the desktop app, a check from your browser, or the command line.">
  <section class="wrap intro">
    <h1>Install Omarchy Mobile</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Three ways onto your phone, each from a signed release. Plug the phone into a computer with a USB cable, and
      the installer checks it, shows exactly what it will write, and writes nothing until you type the phone's
      codename.
    </p>
    <p class="facts">
      <span>Pixel 7 Pro</span>
      <span>Release 2026.11.15 or later</span>
      <span>Stock Android stays on slot A</span>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap block" aria-labelledby="start">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="start">Start here</h2>
      <p>For most people: a window that walks you through it, or a page that checks your phone first.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ways">
      <article class="way">
        <figure class="shot">
          <img
            src="/install/app-reinstall.webp"
            width="900"
            height="720"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="The Omarchy Mobile Installer window asking what is on the phone's slot B, with the choices to install Omarchy Mobile again, Android is on slot B, or not sure."
          />
        </figure>
        <div class="body">
          <p class="kicker">Desktop app</p>
          <h3>Omarchy Mobile Installer</h3>
          <p>
            A desktop app for Linux. It writes the phone, waits for its first start, adds the USB connection, backs
            up the phone's radio partitions, adds the phone's firmware from Google's factory image, restarts it and
            checks it.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Today it reinstalls:</strong> it is for a Pixel 7 Pro that already runs Omarchy Mobile. A first
            install from stock Android uses the <a href="#advanced">command line</a> for now.
          </p>
          <p class="meta">Linux on x86_64: an Arch package for Omarchy and Arch Linux, an AppImage for other distributions.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href={APP_RELEASE}>Download v0.1.0</a>
            <a class="button" href={APP_DOCS}>How to install it</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="way">
        <figure class="shot">
          <img
            src="/install/web-check.webp"
            width="800"
            height="740"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="The web page's first screen: a notice that it cannot write to a phone, the latest release for the Pixel 7 Pro from the release server, and a button to download and check it."
          />
        </figure>
        <div class="body">
          <p class="kicker">In your browser</p>
          <h3>Check your phone and a release</h3>
          <p>
            A page in Chrome, Edge or another Chromium-based browser. It downloads the release and checks its
            signature, looks at your phone over USB, and runs a dry run that lists exactly what an install would
            write.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>It checks; it doesn't install.</strong> Nothing is written to the phone. Installing from the
            browser is coming.
          </p>
          <p class="meta">Nothing you type and no file you pick leaves your computer.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <a class="button primary" href={WEB_APP}>Check your phone</a>
            <a class="button" href="/install/web/">About the page</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap block" aria-labelledby="advanced">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="advanced">Advanced: the command line</h2>
      <p>
        For first installs today, for people at home in a terminal, and for the agent you run. One command from the
        release you download runs the whole install, stops when it needs you, and goes on from where it stopped.
      </p>
    </div>
    <pre class="cmd"><code>cd omamobile-cheetah-&lt;version&gt;
bash install --guided</code></pre>
    <dl class="how">
      <div>
        <dt>The guided install</dt>
        <dd>
          First installs and reinstalls, from the warning to a checked phone. A first install on a Pixel 7 Pro
          still stops at the bootloader check; the guide says what to do.
          {" "}<a href={INSTALL_DOC}>The install guide</a> · <a href={GUIDED_DOC}>How it works</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Step by step</dt>
        <dd>
          The same install by hand: <code>bash install --dry-run</code>, then <code>bash install</code>
          (<code>tools/install-phone</code>), the radio backup and the firmware, each on its own.
          {" "}<a href={`${INSTALL_DOC}#1-unlock-the-bootloader-this-erases-the-phone`}>The steps</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Build it yourself</dt>
        <dd>
          The packages, the system image and the kernel, built from source on your own computer.
          {" "}<a href={`${REPO_URL}#quick-start`}>The repository</a>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap block" aria-labelledby="know">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="know">Before you install</h2>
    </div>
    <dl class="how">
      <div>
        <dt>Installing erases the phone</dt>
        <dd>
          Unlocking the bootloader erases it, and the install replaces its user data. Copy off what you want to keep
          first.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Your way back stays</dt>
        <dd>
          Only the phone's second boot slot and its user data are written. Stock Android stays on the other slot,
          and the bootloader, the radio and the phone's calibration are never touched.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Google's files stay Google's</dt>
        <dd>
          The phone's firmware comes from Google's factory image for your phone, on your own computer. Omarchy
          Mobile never hosts Google's files.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href="/devices/cheetah">What works on the Pixel 7 Pro</a>
      <a class="button" href={`${REPO_URL}/releases`}>Releases</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .intro { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4.5rem) 0; }
  .intro h1 { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(1.0625rem, 1rem + 0.4vw, 1.25rem); color: var(--text-2); max-width: 52ch; }
  .facts { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; max-width: none; }
  .facts span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--text-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 0.25rem 0.6rem;
  }

  .block { padding-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem); }
  .head { display: grid; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .head p { margin: 0; color: var(--text-2); max-width: 70ch; }
  .actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; }

  .ways { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 26rem), 1fr)); gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
  .way {
    display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: calc(var(--radius) * 2); background: var(--surface); overflow: hidden;
  }
  .shot { margin: 0; background: var(--bg-deep); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); padding: clamp(0.75rem, 2vw, 1.25rem); }
  .shot img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 900 / 720; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: var(--radius); outline: 1px solid var(--border-strong); }
  .body { display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 1.75rem); }
  .body p { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .body strong { color: var(--text); }
  .kicker { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--accent); margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .body h3 { font-size: 1.375rem; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.875rem !important; }
  .body .actions { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 0.5rem; }

  .cmd {
    margin: 0 0 2rem; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; overflow-x: auto; max-width: 40rem;
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .cmd code { background: none; padding: 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--text); }

  .how { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 18rem), 1fr)); gap: 2rem 3rem; margin: 0; }
  .how dt { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .how dd { margin: 0; }
</style>
